ref "/athletes/11106"} "Joe Jacobi"] " of the United States. In the second round, both " [:a {:href "/athletes/9407"} "Miroslav Šimek"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9406"} "Jiří Rohan"] " of Czechoslovakia, the 1991 World runners-up, and Adisson and Forgues posted higher scores, but the Americans did not wither to the challenge and managed an even higher score, securing them the gold medal, leaving silver and bronze to Czechoslovakia and France respectively. Loose and Hemmer also bettered their previous mark in this portion of the tournament, but they still sank to 13th in the final rankings."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Total Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "407"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11156"} "Scott Strausbaugh"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/11106"} "Joe Jacobi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "122.41"] [:td {} "124.82 (1)"] [:td {} "122.41 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "414"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9407"} "Miroslav Šimek"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/9406"} "Jiří Rohan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TCH"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TCH.png"}] "TCH"]] [:td {} "124.25"] [:td {} "131.91 (3)"] [:td {} "124.25 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "416"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9589"} "Franck Adisson"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/9629"} "Wilfrid Forgues"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:st